Individual product items within a shopping cart.

Represents specific product variants added to a customer's cart, including the selected quantity and variant details. Each cart can contain multiple items from different products, with validation to prevent adding out-of-stock variants.

Items are managed through the parent cart operations, ensuring consistency during bulk modifications and checkout processes. Stock validation occurs at the time of addition to maintain purchase intent accuracy.

The item records enable complex shopping behaviors like quantity adjustments, variant changes, and partial cart operations without affecting other cart contents.

